{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Determinant.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Perm","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Fin.Basic"],"declarations":37,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.det_gram_map_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.det_gram_map_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":462,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L462-L485","doc":"**The transfer.** An integer matrix with a nonzero `r × r` minor has a\nnonsingular Gram matrix over *every* characteristic-zero field.\n\nThe order is only used over `ℤ`; `k` never needs to be ordered, which is\nexactly what keeps `sp01`'s hypothesis at `[Field k] [CharZero k]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.det_mul_transpose_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.det_mul_transpose_pos","kind":"theorem","line":447,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L447-L454","doc":"**One nonzero minor suffices.** A single nonvanishing `r × r` minor makes\nthe whole Gram determinant strictly positive — the other terms cannot cancel\nit, because they are squares. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.det_mul_transpose_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.det_mul_transpose_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":441,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L441-L445","doc":"A Gram determinant is never negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.det_mul_transpose_eq_sum_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.det_mul_transpose_eq_sum_sq","kind":"theorem","line":427,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L427-L435","doc":"**Gram form.** `det (A Aᵀ)` is the sum of the squares of the `r × r`\nminors of `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.det_mul_eq_sum_minors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.det_mul_eq_sum_minors","kind":"theorem","line":385,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L385-L407","doc":"**Rectangular Cauchy–Binet.** `det (A * B) = ∑_f det (A_f) * det (B^f)`\nover the strictly monotone `f : Fin r → Fin n`.\n\nAbsent from Mathlib as of this writing — see the header note. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.sum_term_eq_sum_pairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.sum_term_eq_sum_pairs","kind":"theorem","line":355,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L355-L383","doc":"**The reindexing.** Sorting is a bijection from the injective `φ` onto the\npairs `(f, π)`, and `Finset.sum_bij'` takes exactly the two round trips proved\nabove plus the factorization.\n\nNote the direction of `sum_bij'`'s `i`: it is allowed to depend on membership,\nwhich is what lets it be `φ ↦ (sortSelector hφ, sortPerm hφ)` — `sortSelector`\nneeds the injectivity proof, so the non-dependent `sum_nbij'` cannot express\nthis map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.mem_injFns_of","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.mem_injFns_of","kind":"theorem","line":351,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L351-L353","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.mem_injFns","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.mem_injFns","kind":"theorem","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L347-L349","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.injFns","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.injFns","kind":"def","line":342,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L342-L345","doc":"The injective `φ` — after `term_eq_zero_of_not_injective`, the only index\nset that carries any weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.sum_term_comp_perm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.sum_term_comp_perm","kind":"theorem","line":325,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L325-L340","doc":"For a fixed selector, summing the term over all permutations gives the\nproduct of the two minors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.term_eq_zero_of_not_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.term_eq_zero_of_not_injective","kind":"theorem","line":319,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L319-L323","doc":"Only injective `φ` can contribute. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.term","kind":"def","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L314-L317","doc":"The summand, named so the reindexing has something to talk about. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.det_submatrix_comp_perm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.det_submatrix_comp_perm","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L295-L302","doc":"**Permuting the columns.** `A.submatrix id (f ∘ π)` is `A.submatrix id f`\nwith its columns shuffled by `π`, so the determinants differ by `sign π`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.sortPerm_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.sortPerm_comp","kind":"theorem","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L286-L293","doc":"**Round trip, permutation half.** Sorting `f ∘ π` recovers `π`, since the\nfactorization pins it and `f` is injective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.sortSelector_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.sortSelector_comp","kind":"theorem","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L274-L284","doc":"**Round trip, selector half.** Sorting `f ∘ π` recovers `f` — because `f`\nis already the increasing enumeration of that image, and\n`Finset.orderEmbOfFin_unique` says there is only one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.comp_perm_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.comp_perm_injective","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L269-L272","doc":"A selector composed with a permutation is injective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.sortSelector_comp_sortPerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.sortSelector_comp_sortPerm","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L256-L267","doc":"**The factorization.** `φ = f ∘ π`, with `f` the sorted selector and `π`\nthe induced permutation — the statement the assembly step needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.sortPerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.sortPerm","kind":"def","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L249-L254","doc":"**The permutation `φ` induces**: where each index lands once the image is\nput in increasing order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.toImage_bijective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.toImage_bijective","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L240-L247","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.toImage","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.toImage","kind":"def","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L236-L238","doc":"`φ` viewed as a map into its own image. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.sortSelector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.sortSelector","kind":"def","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L229-L234","doc":"**The selector `φ` sorts to** — its image enumerated in increasing order.\nStrict monotonicity comes free from `orderEmbOfFin` being an order embedding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.card_imageFinset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.card_imageFinset","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L223-L227","doc":"An injective `φ` has an image of exactly `r` elements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.mem_imageFinset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.mem_imageFinset","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L219-L221","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.imageFinset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.imageFinset","kind":"def","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L215-L217","doc":"The image of `φ`, as a `Finset`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.det_mul_eq_sum_det_submatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.det_mul_eq_sum_det_submatrix","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L197-L204","doc":"**`det (A * B)` as a sum of minors-times-products over all `φ`.** The\nnon-injective terms are already zero by `det_submatrix_eq_zero_of_not_injective`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.sum_over_perms_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.sum_over_perms_eq","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L182-L195","doc":"For every `φ`, the inner `σ`-sum factors as a determinant times the\n`σ`-independent `B` product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.sum_over_perms_eq_zero_of_not_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.sum_over_perms_eq_zero_of_not_injective","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L160-L173","doc":"**Step 3.** A non-injective `φ` contributes `0` to the regrouped sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.det_submatrix_eq_zero_of_not_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.det_submatrix_eq_zero_of_not_injective","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L148-L158","doc":"A repeated column kills it: if `φ` is not injective, `A.submatrix id φ`\nhas two equal columns. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.sum_perm_eq_det_submatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.sum_perm_eq_det_submatrix","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L140-L146","doc":"The `σ`-sum is the determinant of the column-selected submatrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.det_mul_eq_sum_over_functions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.det_mul_eq_sum_over_functions","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L118-L127","doc":"**`det (A * B)` grouped by `φ`.** Every later step is a statement about a\nsingle `φ`: non-injective ones vanish, injective ones factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.prod_sum_interchange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.prod_sum_interchange","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L111-L116","doc":"The product-of-sums, expanded as a sum over `φ : Fin r → Fin n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.det_mul_leibniz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.det_mul_leibniz","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L92-L103","doc":"**Leibniz form.** `det (A * B)` as a signed sum over permutations of a\nproduct of `(A * B)` entries — the starting point, with no rearrangement yet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.mul_apply'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.mul_apply'","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L85-L90","doc":"`(A * B) i j` written out, so the Leibniz expansion has something to\nrewrite with. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.minorB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.minorB","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L72-L75","doc":"The `r × r` minor of `B` on the rows picked by `f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.minorA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.minorA","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L67-L70","doc":"The `r × r` minor of `A` on the columns picked by `f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.instFintypeSelector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.instFintypeSelector","kind":"instance","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L64-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.Selector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CauchyBinet.Selector","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CauchyBinet.lean#L60-L62","doc":"The strictly monotone maps `Fin r → Fin n` — equivalently the `r`-element\nsubsets of `Fin n`, listed in increasing order. These index the minors. ","signatureChunk":0}]}